## 2. Module Responsibilities

The rule that keeps a modular monolith clean over time: **a module should be swappable without the rest of the app noticing.** If you could delete `git/` and drop in a completely different git implementation without touching `repository/`, the boundary is correct.

| Module | Belongs here | Should NEVER be here | Who can call it |
|---|---|---|---|
| `auth/` | Password hashing, JWT logic, session/token validation | Repository or AI logic | `repository/`, `chat/` (to identify the current user) |
| `repository/` | Repository CRUD, state transitions, orchestrating clone + index | Raw git commands, AI calls, HTTP-specific error formatting | Controllers only |
| `git/` | Spawning git processes, clone/delete/pull operations | Prisma calls, knowledge of "repository status", HTTP responses | `repository/` only |
| `indexing/` | File walking, tree-sitter parsing, chunking, embedding generation | Chat conversation logic, HTTP handling | `repository/` (to trigger it), `chat/` (to query it) |
| `chat/` | Conversation state, retrieval orchestration, prompt assembly | Raw provider SDK calls, embedding generation logic | Controllers only |
| `ai/` | Provider interface + implementations | Business logic about repositories or chats | `indexing/`, `chat/` |
| `jobs/` | Queue definitions, job scheduling, worker entrypoints | Business logic itself (jobs call services, they don't reimplement them) | `repository/`, `indexing/` (as producers) |
| `utils/` | Pure functions: parsing, formatting, path building | Database calls, network calls, business decisions | Anyone |
| `common/` | Error classes, shared types, generic middleware | Module-specific logic | Anyone |

The single most important rule in this table: **`git/` should not know Prisma exists, and `repository/` should not know how `git clone` actually works.** That boundary is what lets you swap local cloning for a sandboxed container-based clone later without touching a single line of `RepositoryService`.

